<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  The iOS and iPadOS bundle's properties, configured when the build is configured
  (platforms/ios/CMakeLists.txt). The game is landscape: an iPhone takes the two landscape
  orientations; an iPad takes all four, because iPadOS letterboxes a landscape-only app in a
  portrait screen, and the game turns its own view in a portrait screen instead
  (src/ios_platform.mm). Full screen on every device with no status bar, the icon the asset
  compiler makes (CFBundleIcons names its files), no encryption beyond the system's own, the
  local network wording for LAN games, the Documents folder visible in the Files app and the
  Finder, a mouse or trackpad read as a pointer, the type of the game's archives (.hpi,
  .ufo, .ccx and .gp3 files), which the Game files screen's picker offers when the player adds
  archives (src/ios_game_files.mm), and the eight file types as the app's own, which it opens
  as each type's owner from the Files app and the share sheet (src/ios_platform.mm): a mod
  package (.oamod), a language pack (.oalang), a map pack (.oamap), a mutator package
  (.oamut), a brain package (.oabrain), a key layout package (.oakeys), a registry file
  (.oareg) and a launch file
  (.oalaunch). Each of the first seven
  conforms to public.data, not
  public.zip-archive or public.archive, so that nothing unpacks a package as a zip instead of
  handing it to the game, and a browser downloads a registry file rather than showing it; a
  launch file is text, and conforms to public.plain-text. iOS draws each icon from the app's
  icon.
-->
